# GuardTalkOS — gs201_tangorpro (gs201 / tangorpro-kernels 6.1) canonical vendor_dlkm blocklist.
#
# T-PORT-TANGORPRO-EXCISION-VARIANT (P1) — DEC-PORT-TANGORPRO-002 / -003.
#
# Derivation (mechanical, no invented entries — every upstream line verbatim and
# in order, then ONE GuardTalk addition that is proven present on this device):
#   upstream device/google/tangorpro-kernels/6.1/grapheneos/vendor_dlkm.modules.blocklist
#   + 'blocklist nitrous' (T-BT-FULL FR-3): nitrous.ko IS loaded on this device —
#     device/google/tangorpro-kernels/6.1/grapheneos/vendor_dlkm.modules.load
#     contains extra/private/google-modules/bluetooth/broadcom/nitrous.ko
#
# Deliberately NOT present (do not "fix" by copying a phone row):
#   * bcmdhd4383 / bcmdhd4390 / bcmdhd4398 — tangorpro loads NO bcmdhd*.ko. Its
#     Wi-Fi driver is synadhd.ko (wlan/dhd43752p), which is NOT blocklisted.
#   * syna_touch / focal_touch / goodix_brl_touch / sec_touch — tangorpro's load
#     list carries nvt_touch.ko and blocks no touch driver.
#   * cpif / cpif_page / shm_ipc — the baseband IPC transport does not exist on
#     this device: there is no modem hardware (no radio.img, no
#     `require version-baseband=` in firmware/android-info.txt). The RIL userspace
#     (google-ril, radioext) is excised at the PACKAGE layer instead.
#
# Devices mapped to this variant: see excision-variants.mk GT_DEVICE_VARIANT_tangorpro.
# Re-verify with the derivation commands in
# .agent-comm/evidence/T-PORT-TANGORPRO-EXCISION-VARIANT/derive-row.sh

blocklist aoc_unit_test_dev
blocklist mali_kutf
blocklist mali_kutf_clk_rate_trace_test_portal
blocklist rt4539_bl
blocklist sscoredump_sample_test.ko
blocklist sscoredump_test.ko

# T-BT-FULL (FR-3): Bluetooth power/rfkill driver — BCM BT on UART.
blocklist nitrous
